AB  - The proceedings contain 11 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Experiences and Directions. The topics include: Parsing native OWL DL into executable ontologies in an object oriented paradigm; healthy lifestyle support; an experimental evaluation of automatically generated multiple choice questions from ontologies; use cases and suitability metrics for unit ontologies; a simplified agile methodology for ontology development; using ontology design patterns to represent sustainability indicator sets; collaborative ontology evolution and data quality - an empirical analysis; application of inference rules to a software requirements ontology to generate software test cases; towards ontology-based event processing; minimal coverage for ontology signatures; OWL API for iOS; early implementation and results.
