AB  - The proceedings contain 29 papers. The special focus in this conference is on The Mobile Learning Voyage - From Small Ripples to Massive Open Waters. The topics include: Using mobile devices in supervision of graduate research in distance education; technology integration in diverse contexts; transforming teaching and learning; rhizomatic principles in mlearning; mobile learning in a flipped multimedia higher education classroom; infinite possibilities for using eyetracking for mobile serious games in order to improve user learning experiences; a mobile game world for maori language learning; using SNSs to promote STEMI on the backseat of a taxi across Africa; the ship has left the harbour, but the captain is MIA; use of web 2.0 and mobile technologies for developing argumentative skills; journey of self-determination; facilitating knowledge visualisation as communication and knowledge transfer mechanism in postgraduate learning; developing a sense of identity as a governor within a mobile learning community; small talk versus smart talk; designs for heritage language learning; introducing an ipad innovation into accounting tutorials; challenges of using a location-based mobile learning platform; influencing everyday teacher practices by applying mobile digital storytelling as a seamless learning approach; towards design patterns for augmented reality serious games; the adoption of mobile technologies in a higher education institution; heutagogial approaches in the understanding and modelling the adoption of mobile learning; learning with wearable technologies and difficulties experienced by students using mobile devices to access e-learning.
