AB  - In the last two years, the authors' research has been focused on designing a smart solution to compensate for hearing or visual deficiencies using the Google Glass hardware device and its own software architecture. The testing has shown that the solution is beneficial and can now be tested and used in practice. Education has been selected as one of the appropriate areas for testing. This paper describes the combination of Google Glass and the educational application called English Today. The application English Today is used by the students on mobile phones on platforms Android and iOS. There is a brief explanation of the architecture of the designed solution, a description of the user interface through Google Glass. The use of the application English Today and Google Glass and its general architecture appears to be beneficial and opens new opportunities for education hearing or visually impaired people. © 2019 IEEE.
