AD  - Kazakh -British Technical University, St.Tole 59, Almaty, Kazakhstan
AB  - Nowadays the detection of abnormal situations in the process of functioning of information systems is a very important task in emerging technologies and applications. The basic problems of financial organizations are the increasing number of clients, improvement of financial products and services, and anomaly detection in corporate information systems which influence productivity, reliability, and availability. The aim of the work is to develop a framework of network and system behavior for corporate information systems and suggest an approach for detecting anomalies in the test case of issuing virtual cards. In our paper we apply the next techniques, we build the architecture of anomaly detection on Business Process Modelling Notation (BPMN). We use the UML tool sequence diagram by describing the business process of issuing virtual cards. We implement software tools: database, programming language, and datasets. We test the development on mobile technologies (iOS, Android). Our brief finding is concluded by decreasing the number of anomalies in the test case of issuing virtual cards. Our contribution to paper is that we build web services that can effectively solve the problems of big data queries. The novelty is based on our suggestion of application architecture of anomaly detection using a Machine learning module. We apply our architecture model in the process of issuing virtual cards. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
