AD  - Department of Architecture, National University of Singapore, Singapore
AD  - Division of Industrial Design, National University of Singapore, Singapore
AD  - Smart System Institute, National University of Singapore, Singapore
AB  - This paper positions spatial computing not as a visualization endpoint, but as an active site of design reasoning within generative architectural workflows. Using custom applications for Apple Vision Pro and iPad, we introduce a multimodal system that enables designers to move fluidly between 2D sketching, AI-driven 3D generation, and immersive 1:1 spatial evaluation. Through three studies with architecture students and expert practitioners, we investigate how embodied interaction—walking through, around, and inside AIgenerated forms—reshapes design judgement, proportion decisions, and spatial intuition. Our findings show that while tablet-based interaction accelerates idea generation and refinement, spatial immersion enables deeper perceptual understanding of mass, light, and enclosure, influencing design choices beyond what screen-based tools afford. By analysing how designers negotiate authorship, agency, and iteration across platforms, this paper contributes new knowledge to spatial computing in architectural ideation and argues that generative AI gains its full potential only when situated within embodied spatial experience. © 2026 and published by the Association for Computer-Aided Architectural Design Research in Asia (CAADRIA), Hong Kong.
