AB  - This paper describes our work to improve how IBM employees install IBM mobile apps through the design and development of a native IBM App Store for iOS. Using established UX design techniques such as usability testing and user surveys, we redesigned a legacy hybrid app to have a clean, modern interface leveraging Apples’ latest iOS design patterns, and introduced a visual hierarchy that keeps the experience focused on the core user tasks. The improved app allows users to find and install apps more quickly, through an engaging UX that users prefer. © Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2020.
