TI  - From Policy to Practice: An Investigation of the Apple App Store Account Deletion Requirements
PY  - 2026
T2  - IEEE Software
DO  - 10.1109/MS.2026.3730641
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105050475644?origin=resultslist
AD  - Louisiana State University, United States
AB  - On June 30, 2022, the Apple App Store enforced a new policy requiring that apps that support account creation must also support user-initiated account deletion. The policy is intended to grant end-users control over their data. However, the influence of such a policy on the state of practice is yet to be explored. Understanding how platform policies shape the mobile app landscape is crucial for evaluating their effectiveness and improving practitioner compliance. To address this gap, we qualitatively analyze the account deletion option of 50 iOS apps. In addition, we interview 14 practitioners to gain insight into their perceptions of the policy. Our results show that apps often employ dark design patterns to deter users from deleting their accounts. The results also highlight practitioners? concerns about the clarity, effectiveness, and fairness of the policy. Based on our findings, we propose strategies to help improve the effectiveness of the policy and promote compliance. © 1984-2012 IEEE.
