AB  - This paper presents CloudTunnel VPN, a production-grade, cross-platform virtual private network system implemented in a Flutter client interface and Next.js service backend that provides high-performance secure tunneling using the WireGuard protocol. It uses modern cryptographic primitives, including Curve25519 for key exchange and ChaCha20-Poly1305 for authenticated encryption, to ensure strong confidentiality and integrity guarantees. The evaluation shows that our CloudTunnel VPN achieves up to 92% of baseline throughput at 87.1 Mbps with merely 6 ms latency overhead and preserves perfect forward secrecy. It represents 45% improvement over OpenVPN-based counterparts since The WireGuard handshakes complete in 187 ms. It also integrates Better-Auth authentication, PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM, Redis caching, and automated server-side configuration generation to facilitate its secure deployment. Cross-platform compilation will enable it to seamlessly work on Android, iOS, Windows, macOS, and Linux with one single Flutter codebase. Security assessment shows its resilience against MITM attacks, DNS leaks, and replay attacks via layered defense-in-depth mechanisms. Real-world deployment reports 99.7% uptime for the service, consistent IP obfuscation, and automated cryptographic key-rotation capabilities. © 2026 IEEE.
