N1  - Funding text 1: The Formation Flying of CubeSat Assembly for Remote Sensing (FORCE) project, which concluded in January 2023, lies in this context of growing interest toward small-satellite missions with higher autonomy and servicing capabilities. The project, funded by the Italian Ministry of University and Research, was led by the Department of Industrial Engineering of the University of Naples \u201CFederico II\u201D and involved a large consortium of academic and industrial entities [40]. The project proposed a new mission concept involving a fleet of modular formation-flying (FF) 12U CubeSats with a 4U \u00D7 3U \u00D7 1U form factor to implement FF Synthetic Aperture Radar observation modes at low cost and with a short time development cycle. One of the major project goals was the design and realization of functioning prototype subsystem modules conceived to support such a mission concept. The work in this paper focuses on the relative positioning (RELPOS) module prototype, conceived to provide a 12U servicing platform with accurate relative navigation capabilities for close-range inspection and rendezvous toward satellites of the FORCE fleet. The latter are designed as semi-cooperative targets, hosting a set of NIR-reflecting circular markers on one of their faces. The RELPOS module employs a laser range finder (LRF) and a monocular camera, both operating in the near-infrared (NIR) bandwidth, to detect the markers and use them as reference features for pose estimation. The LRF emitter is characterized by a relatively large beam divergence, thus also acting as an illuminator to irradiate the markers. The sensors are integrated with a dedicated single-board computer (SBC) so as to make the overall RELPOS design occupy at most two CubeSat units.
N1  - Funding text 2: The authors would like to thank Professor Salvatore Amoruso from the Department of Physics \u201CEttore Pancini\u201D of the University of Naples \u201CFederico II\u201D and Dr. Guido Di Donfrancesco and Mr. Pasquale Castellano from Advanced Lidar Applications (ALA) S.r.l. for the design and development of the laser range-finder unit and the related software.
