AB  - We examine the hardware components and software tools that determine the architectural framework of smartphone-based point-of-care biosensing platforms. Important hardware interfacing concepts, identification of data payloads from sensors, and processes of directing them to specific applications are detailed. Various classes in the Android Sensor application programming interfaces, commonly used sensor types, Sensor Manager Library, and sensor data management are discussed. Important protocols and software structure of physical connectors like the USB On-the-Go is compared with wireless sensor interfacing methods like near-field communication and Bluetooth. Model-view-controller design pattern, iOS app programming frameworks including widely used classes and iOS developer libraries for sensor data capture are discussed. © 2022 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
