AB  - Public interactive displays are widely used across urban settings, yet many existing systems still rely on fixed setups, support only a narrow range of devices, and offer limited simple interaction techniques (e.g. binary voting). As deployments scale and attract more diverse users, such limitations make sustained collaboration difficult and expose unresolved systems challenges in concurrency, cross-device synchronization, and the management of long-running shared state. We present Pixelate, a platform-independent collaborative drawing system for public displays. Pixelate uses a cloud-backed, event-driven architecture to support distributed shared state collaboration across custom web, Android, and iOS clients. It enables persistent canvas state, real-time synchronization, and application-layer concurrency control for multi-user interaction.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
