AB  - The popularity of GPGPUs in high performance platforms for scientific computing in recent times has renewed interest in approximate inverse preconditioners for Krylov methods. We have recently introduced some new algorithmic variants [6] of popular approximate inverse methods. We now report on the behaviour of these variations in high performance multilevel preconditioning frameworks, and we present the software framework that enables us to easily deal with heterogeneous computing platforms that include GPGPUs. © 2014 The authors and IOS Press.
